# Install on a real Android device when the chat finishes

Before the closing reply of a chat that changed the Android app, build the debug APK and install it on the connected physical device, then launch it.

## When to run

Run this when the chat is done and files under `android-native/` changed. Skip chats that only answered a question or only edited docs, rules, or research notes.

## Steps

1. List devices with `adb devices -l`.
2. Use a physical device. Its serial does not start with `emulator-`.
3. If no physical device is connected, say so in the closing reply and stop. Do not install on an emulator for this step.
4. From `android-native/`, build, install, and launch:

```bash
./gradlew assembleDebug
adb -s <serial> install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
adb -s <serial> shell am start -n com.micorlov.videopoker/com.micorlov.videopoker.nativeapp.MainActivity
```

5. Confirm install printed `Success` and the activity started. Name the device serial in the closing reply.

If the build or install fails, put the error in the closing reply. Do not say the phone was updated.
